# Git commits

Adapted from awesome-cursorrules conventional-commit rule. Only commit when the
user explicitly asks.

## Format

```text
<type>(optional-scope): <short imperative summary>

Optional body: why, not what. Reference docs/ADR/milestone when relevant.
```

Common types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `test`, `refactor`, `chore`, `ci`.

## Examples

- `feat(annotation): build five-role GRCh38 graph from GENCODE v38`
- `fix(matrix): reject genome-build mismatch in manifest`
- `docs(plans): record milestone 3 static-feature export plan`

## Do not

- Update git config, force-push, or amend unless the user's commit rules allow.
- Commit secrets, `.env`, credentials, or large raw data under `data/`.
